diff --git a/doc/execution-semantics.md b/doc/execution-semantics.md
index c59bab4b3f..648d478869 100644
--- a/doc/execution-semantics.md
+++ b/doc/execution-semantics.md
@@ -304,7 +304,13 @@ and the user need not certify infrastructure state in a reconciliation form.
 
 Repeated automatic signals for an unchanged gate share one durable skipped-wake diagnostic, scoped to company, agent, issue, gate code, and condition identity. The diagnostic retains the first request and counts later observations. This applies to execution reconciliation, dependencies, pause holds, company and agent availability, budget blocks, and disabled heartbeats. These diagnostics do not consume provider attempts and are never proof that a future wake was delivered. All current gates are checked again on the next wake, including the periodic dependency reconciliation sweep. Clearing one gate does not bypass another.
 
-New comments received during an execution hold retain their individual deferred receipts and ordered comment ids. Release cannot drain those receipts while replay remains blocked; the next eligible wake can adopt them. Authorized external-chat requests also remain deferred with their exact durable receipt. They must use normal promotion and current authorization; a generic wake cannot adopt only their comment ids and discard their actor or session contract. A wait does not authorize replay, reset an incident retry budget, or bypass an interaction's delivery rules.
+A wake whose only gate is the previous execution's unreleased process or environment lease (`execution_owner_active` without a recovery action) is saved input, not a diagnostic: a handoff or stage wake blocked there is the only notification its recipient will get. Admission parks it as a deferred receipt; repeated signals from one requester merge into that receipt. When the executor that held the lease finishes cleanup, the receipt re-enters ordinary admission with its own identity, so every current gate still applies and the receipt is consumed with its successor run. A run of the same agent admitted on that task in the meantime adopts the receipt instead; a receipt whose task closed, changed owner, or moved to another stage participant, or whose agent already started a later run on the task, retires without a run. Chat conversations keep their existing turn rules.
+
+Ownership-wait recovery uses the shared delivery-work coordinator. Admission registers a notification before writing the receipt in its transaction; outer settlement wakes the worker. Startup reconstructs existing receipts, and a bounded retry remains scheduled at the oldest receipt's 30-second retry deadline only while receipts remain pending. Paused companies retain their pending obligation. Empty queues and completed history schedule no scans, and ordinary heartbeat ticks do not inspect this queue. Drain retains admitted notifications without database polling; resume and shutdown use the shared lifecycle. Notifications follow the existing single-active-writer contract: independent SQL/process writers need an explicit wake integration, while startup still reconstructs durable state. This does not establish cross-replica notification delivery or deployed host sleep.
+
+Resume reads the current receipt under the task lock rather than replaying the sweep's snapshot. Admission checks that exact payload and current stage again; a concurrent merged signal stays deferred for the next pass. Adoption uses the same owner/stage eligibility and carries the applicable stage's role, review instructions, and allowed actions into the successor's wake context. Obsolete or conflicting stage instructions are not adopted.
+
+New comments received during an execution hold retain their individual deferred receipts and ordered comment ids. The ownership-wait merge and sweep exclude comments, interrupts, task Retry requests, interaction continuations, and native status receipts before selecting a batch or changing retry timestamps, even when those receipts name the same execution hold. Release cannot drain those receipts while replay remains blocked; the next eligible wake can adopt them. Authorized external-chat requests also remain deferred with their exact durable receipt. They must use normal promotion and current authorization; a generic wake cannot adopt only their comment ids and discard their actor or session contract. A wait does not authorize replay, reset an incident retry budget, or bypass an interaction's delivery rules.
 
 The conversation groups repeated empty pre-start reconciliation cancellations into a neutral waiting notice. Started runs, actual startup failures, and run history remain inspectable. No historical run records are deleted.
 
